>> title: Sourdough Boule
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, sourdough, starter, oven, overnight
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: sourdough, pain au levain, country loaf
>> pairs-with: new-england-clam-chowder
>> servings: 12
>> time: 24 hr
>> slack: narrow — the night in the banneton is the slack; the bulk is not, and an over-proofed dough bakes flat however well you score it
>> step.1: whisk smooth
>> step.2: add flour, rest 45 min
>> step.3: work in the salt, fold every 45 min for 4 hours
>> step.4: shape a boule, dust, chill overnight in a banneton
>> step.5: score, bake in a Dutch oven 500°F 20 min covered + 450°F 25 min open

Whisk @active sourdough starter{1/2%cup}(100 g) into @warm water{1 1/2%cup}(350 g).

Add @bread flour{3 1/4%cup}(450 g) and @whole wheat flour{1/2%cup}(50 g) to @&(~1)slurry{}, then rest ~{45%min}.

Work @fine sea salt{2%tsp}(10 g) into @&(~1)dough{}, folding every ~{45%min}.

Shape @&(~1)dough{} into a boule, dust with @rice flour{2%Tbs}, and chill in a #banneton{} for ~{14%hours}.

Score @&(~1)loaf{} and bake in a #Dutch oven{} at 500°F for ~{20%min} covered, then at 450°F for ~{25%min} uncovered.
